' ============================================================
' DESIGN NOTES
' ============================================================
note bottom of RenderGroupSerializer
  **Why compute in the serializer (vs DB view)?**
  • Single source of truth for the formula across
    list / detail / future cost endpoints.
  • Lets ``end = now`` for running tasks without
    a SQL recompute.
  • Already does this shape for ``progress_pct``.
  • Pure read-side; no migration risk.
end note

note bottom of Ticker
  **Why a hook (not server polling)?**
  Running-task actuals are a closed-form function
  of ``started_at`` (immutable) + ``price`` (immutable)
  + ``now``.  Polling the server every second
  would burn ~80 req/s during a busy group.
  The ticker re-renders locally; the next real
  poll already gives canonical actuals on completion.
end note

note left of Bootstrap
  **No backend schema migration.**
  All three columns and their write paths
  exist today.  P2 is purely about exposing
  them + fixing community pricing.

  Net backend diff: ~25 lines across 4 files.
end note

